{{also|tha|THA|-tha|þa|thá|thả}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|gem-pro|*þawō}}. The conclusive -n has fallen away in the Scandinavian dialects already in the oldest texts.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈθauː/}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv}}

# [[then]], the past
#: {{ux|is|'''Þá''' var ég ungur maður.|'''Then''' I was a young man.}}
# [[then]]
#* Genesis 5:3 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20bók%20Móse+5:3&version=ICELAND Icelandic], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%205:3&version=NIV English])
#*: {{ux|is|Adam lifði hundrað og þrjátíu ár. '''Þá''' gat hann son í líking sinni, eftir sinni mynd, og nefndi hann Set.|When Adam had lived 130 years, '''then''' he had a son in his own likeness, in his own image; and he named him Seth.}}
#: {{ux|is|'''Þá''' fer ég bara!|'''Then''' I'll just leave!}}
#: {{ux|is|Hvað gerirðu '''þá'''?|What will you do '''then'''?}}

